# There and back again: an ester is made, then unmade.
# Acid and alcohol condense to an ester and water; the same ester,
# met with hydroxide, hydrolyses back to the alcohol and the acid's
# salt. Two curated transformations, each proven against an
# atom-mapped template — and each one runs only when asked, because
# a beaker of vinegar and spirit does not do this by itself.
add v1 CH3COOH 0.1mol
add v1 ethanol 0.1mol
react v1 esterification
look v1
add v1 NaOH 0.1mol
react v1 saponification
register lv3
inspect v1
